    "body": "While looking into #36759 I discovered `-notorcontrol` did the opposite of what would be expected from it and I then checked for similar issues in other init options. There are several more where `-nofoo` does something surprising including one of them crashing the node.\r\n\r\nThis PR attempts to fix all these surprising behaviors while also keeping things as simple as possible and just change behavior to something that makes sense harmless in the context of the option. Fixes that use a common approach for the fix are grouped together into a commit even if the options included themselves may have no relation at all.\r\n\r\n| Commit | Problematic options behavior | Fix approach |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| [mempool: Reject cluster limits below 1](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/512773d111daaa4330c873ed5889b9ef511f6e3a) | `-nolimitclustercount` hits an assertion in `TxGraph` on the first mempool transaction. `-nolimitclustersize` rejects every transaction. | Reject values below 1 at startup. |\r\n| [args: Make negation a no-op for options that are off by default](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/5d2ddcae41522a0651e20476b7481ea2e50a6fcb) | `GetArg()` returns `\"0\"` for a negated option. The `-no*notify` options run the command `0`, `-nosigner` uses `0` as signer, `-noi2psam` fails startup and `-norpcpassword` sets the password to `0`. Opt-in because options like `-noonion` and `-noblockfilterindex` depend on reading `\"0\"`. | New opt-in flag `NEGATE_TO_DEFAULT` makes `GetArg()` return the default. |\r\n| [init: Read -cjdnsreachable and -help as booleans](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/08b4f855104b7ef25b82d66447b9e502c9bef5e9) | `-cjdnsreachable=0` and `-nocjdnsreachable` turn CJDNS on. `-nohelp` prints the help. | Use `GetBoolArg()` instead of `IsArgSet()`. |\r\n| [args, wallet: Treat empty -blocksdir and -walletdir as unset](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/cd5bfc823063f5d06e8a15180ba05e2afc7506fb) | `-noblocksdir` writes block files relative to the working directory. `-nowalletdir` fails startup. | Fall back to the default directory, like `-datadir` does. |\r\n| [init: Disable the automatic onion service with -notorcontrol](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/faf0a220338cbff2e045f0535635590f2d33fbe2) | `-notorcontrol` connects to `0.0.0.0:9051`, which reaches a local Tor. | Set `-listenonion=0`. |\r\n| [init: Disallow negating options where it has no meaning](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/4b181fd471f2826659e000439f10345a483309f4) | `-nobantime`, `-nocheckblocks`, `-nomaxreceivebuffer`, `-nomaxsendbuffer` and `-nomaxtipage` read as 0, the opposite of what the user asked for. | Fail at startup with `DISALLOW_NEGATION`. |\r\n\r\n`-nomempoolexpiry` has a similar kind of problem. It evicts transactions as soon as the next one arrives. I left it out because #36540 already is open and addresses this.",
