      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree ed5eb4a835316038427d1aab8202800352c8be93\nparent 512773d111daaa4330c873ed5889b9ef511f6e3a\nauthor Fabian Jahr <fjahr@protonmail.com> 1794491796 +0100\ncommitter Fabian Jahr <fjahr@protonmail.com> 1794491796 +0100\n\nargs: Make negation a no-op for options that are off by default\n\nGetArg() returns \"0\" for a negated option, so -noblocknotify, -nowalletnotify, -nostartupnotify and -noalertnotify ran the command \"0\", -nosigner used \"0\" as the signer command, -noi2psam failed at startup and -norpcpassword set the RPC password to \"0\" instead of using cookie authentication. Add a NEGATE_TO_DEFAULT flag that makes GetArg() return the default instead and use it for these options as well as -rpcuser and -torpassword. The flag is opt-in because other options such as -noonion and -noblockfilterindex rely on reading \"0\".\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\nComment: GPGTools - https://gpgtools.org\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQTFUcepXIa22ULFLs8UX1meznDSbAUCavXFlBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQFF9Zns5w0mwdZQD/ZmvVRTtK24rOfrLrdNPa\n+A0Ro1LhFGhS4QKasOpk6ZMA/1GisM9He3c8glEsIq7tFOKXR6ooL6NPxszCwoqS\nWH0C\n=zbmy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
