      "message": "args: Make negation a no-op for options that are off by default\n\nGetArg() returns \"0\" for a negated option, so -noblocknotify, -nowalletnotify, -nostartupnotify and -noalertnotify ran the command \"0\", -nosigner used \"0\" as the signer command, -noi2psam failed at startup and -norpcpassword set the RPC password to \"0\" instead of using cookie authentication. Add a NEGATE_TO_DEFAULT flag that makes GetArg() return the default instead and use it for these options as well as -rpcuser and -torpassword. The flag is opt-in because other options such as -noonion and -noblockfilterindex rely on reading \"0\".",
